      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name, originally “Tehichipa,” dates back to the 1860s when settlers called it Williamsburg before adopting the native name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
