      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Tehachapi Loop, a 1,210‑foot spiral track, was engineered in the 1870s to connect the Southern Pacific Railroad’s San Joaquin and Mojave lines.",
